<title>GERMANY: FACT SHEET-Star Alliance the work of five airlines.</title>
<headline>FACT SHEET-Star Alliance the work of five airlines.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is information about the airlines that have formally joined the &quot;Star Alliance&quot; announced on Wednesday in Frankfurt.</p>
<p>The alliance partners are Deutsche Lufthansa AG, United Airlines, SAS, Air Canada and Thai International Airways Ltd.</p>
<p>Brazilian airline Varig said on Wednesday it would join the alliance in October.</p>
<p>STAR ALLIANCE</p>
<p>    Total revenues	     $42.3 billion</p>
<p>    Annual passengers	  174.2 million</p>
<p>    Employees		    210,849</p>
<p>    Cities served		578</p>
<p>Revenue passenger miles  229.3 billion</p>
<p>    Daily departures	   6,233</p>
<p>    Countries served	   106</p>
<p>    Fleet			  1,334 aircraft</p>
<p>UNITED AIRLINES</p>
<p>    Total revenues	     $16.4 billion</p>
<p>    Annual passengers	  82 million</p>
<p>    Employees		    86,458</p>
<p>    Cities served		320</p>
<p>Revenue passenger miles  116.6 billion</p>
<p>    Daily departures	   2,245</p>
<p>    Countries served	   32</p>
<p>    Fleet			  566 aircraft</p>
<p>Major hub airports: Chicago, Denver, San Francisco,</p>
<p>				Washington D.C.</p>
